	(text "Open-collector translators (BSS138), one per wired-OR line. FPGA side pulled to 3.3 V (10 k). No bus-side pull-up: the N8VEM S-100 backplane v4 active terminator already holds these lines at 2.7 V through 270 ohm. The FPGA drives '0' or 'Z' only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 122 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1c28a3ce-4022-450b-a0fc-ace78a53fe41")
	)
	(text "Pin 98 ERROR* and pin 99 POC* are not on that terminator, so only those two keep a 2.2 k pull-up to 5 V. MWRT and SSW_DSB* are inputs to the FPGA. IMSAI: pin 53 is SSW DSB* (front panel forces data onto the processor bus), not ground. RDY = PRDY, XRDY = front panel RUN/STOP, SLAVE_CLR* = EXT CLR, RESET* = PRESET."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 126 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0d2d553a-b53d-44a6-83e0-e7833292d200")
	)
